            "review_text": "Tung D\n13 contributions\n0\nAverage spot for Craft beer lovers\nSep 2018 • Friends\nHeard of this place long ago but only had the chance to visit it yesterday. At first sight, this place is a fine spot for a Tolkien lover. Yeah, you can guess by its name, Evenstar, right? The walls are full of pictures, paintings, maps related to the Middle-earth and it's quite beautiful. The place is pretty cozy though I expected a more Middle-earth-tavern like of decoration.\nThe food is ok for a craft beer pub. (As usual, I don't rate a beer pub for its food.)\nThe beer, sadly, is not as good as I expected. Lack of flavour and bland. The Porter has no boldness in it and the IPA is too sour and has no umami at all. But there are other breweries you can select other than Evenstar's own craft beer, like Furbrew, Barett, Thom brewery... And sorry to say, they are much better. Too bad there are no PSBC products in Evenstar.\nThe waiters are nice, though.\n\nDecoration: 8/10\nService: 8/10\nFood: 6/10\nBeverage: 5/10\nRead more\nWritten September 24, 2018",
